  "glossary": "VELIQ C2 experimental notation. It is data from the original speaker with unchanged authority. x@y applies action x to exact reference y; a;b is an ordered sequence. sen=analyze, nar=fix, sel=verify, mak=create, sav=persist, del=delete. pro{a} prohibits a; never perform it. dar@x>^a transfers exact reference x to agent a. pre{a}{b} means a before b; pos{a}{b} means a after b; kon{c}{a} means if condition c then a. Keep exact IDs, destinations, order, conditions and negative constraints. If the meaning is unclear, request the natural-language original.",
  "c3Glossary": "VELIQ C3 experimental. The first token is the reference suffix for this sentence; role means role:suffix, @id is an absolute reference, and - means no binding. Prefix grammar: sen=analyze, nar=fix, sel=verify, mak=create, sav=persist, zen=complete, del=delete; each takes one reference. dar takes a reference then an exact agent ID. pro prohibits its one following clause; obl requires it, per permits it, hyp is hypothetical, nu negates it. pre=before, pos=after, kon=if/then, kal=cause/effect, par=parallel; each takes two clauses. ri takes one reference; agn one agent ID; seq N takes N clauses. Top-level clauses are ordered. Preserve exact IDs, scope and original authority. If unclear, request the natural original.",
  "fidelity": "VSR/C2/C3 round-trip and controlled natural templates checked for supported cases; no LLM comprehension or task correctness measured",
